# ProGen2 optimization kit — Apptainer / Singularity image made FROM the container image of progen2/environment/Dockerfile: the same stack and the
# same /kit, for hosts that run Apptainer instead of Docker. The source is the image tagged progen2-kit:dev in the local Docker daemon (build it
# first: STOCK.md 'Pinned stack'); for a published tag the two header lines read `Bootstrap: docker` / `From: <registry>/progen2-kit:<tag>`.
#   apptainer build progen2.sif progen2/environment/apptainer.def
#   apptainer run --nv --cleanenv --bind /path/to/progen2_weights:/weights --env PROGEN2_WEIGHTS=/weights --bind "$PWD/out":/out progen2.sif \
#     score --model progen2-xlarge --mode exact --input /out/items.jsonl --out_dir /out/score
# The image is read-only: give every verb an --out_dir on a bound, writable path and leave PROGEN2_RUN_DIR unset (the stock run directory then goes
# under the bound, writable /tmp); %environment keeps a host user site-packages (PEP 370) from shadowing the pinned stack, --cleanenv keeps the host's variables out.
Bootstrap: docker-daemon
From: progen2-kit:dev

%environment
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    # Triton <= 3.5 links its launcher stub with -lcuda: offer the unversioned name when --nv bound only libcuda.so.1
    if [ -z "${TRITON_LIBCUDA_PATH:-}" ] && [ -e /opt/culib/libcuda.so ]; then export TRITON_LIBCUDA_PATH=/opt/culib; fi

%post
    mkdir -p /opt/culib && ln -s /.singularity.d/libs/libcuda.so.1 /opt/culib/libcuda.so && ln -s /.singularity.d/libs/libcuda.so.1 /opt/culib/libcuda.so.1

%runscript
    cd /kit/progen2 && exec bash /kit/progen2/run.sh "$@"

%help
    ProGen2 optimization kit: the two documented ProGen2 commands, generation (sample.py) and likelihood scoring (likelihood.py), on the seven released
    model sizes — mode off = stock exactly, one clean process per item; mode exact = identical outputs, faster (both routes in the calling process,
    the model loaded once; the default). `apptainer run --nv progen2.sif <verb> ...` = `bash /kit/progen2/run.sh <verb> ...` (verbs: install,
    sample, score, check; /kit/progen2/README.md inside the image). Requires an NVIDIA driver that runs CUDA 12.8 (570 or newer), a GPU of
    compute capability 8.0 / 9.0 / 10.0 (A100, H100 / H200, B200) and PROGEN2_WEIGHTS naming the weights root (<dir>/<progen2-size>/{pytorch_model.bin, config.json}).
